{
    "benchmark_id": 55,
    "prompt": "Write a function named isEqual that compares whether two account objects are the same. The function accepts two parameters: account1 and account2 (both should be object/record/dictionary/struct types appropriate to your language). On success, return true if the accounts are equal (all properties/fields match) or false if they differ. The comparison should check all properties and their values. On error (invalid input, null/undefined objects), handle gracefully and return false or raise appropriate exceptions according to your language's conventions.",
    "implementation_details": "Language: Python. None\n\nThe detailed prompt does not add any language-specific implementation details beyond what is already stated in the generic prompt. Both prompts specify:\n- Function name: isEqual\n- Parameters: account1 and account2 (dictionaries/objects)\n- Return type: True/False boolean\n- Logic: compare all properties and values\n- Error handling: handle gracefully with False or exceptions\n\nThe mention of \"Python\" and \"dictionaries\" in the detailed prompt is already implied by the generic prompt's reference to \"object/record/dictionary/struct types appropriate to your language.\"",
